[{"id":"mux-predict-mux4","itemId":"multiplexer","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"The testbench joins bit 0 of its vector <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> to <code class=\"nobreak\">d0</code>, bit 1 to <code class=\"nobreak\">d1</code>, and so on. Here <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> stays at 6, which is 0110: <code class=\"nobreak\">d3</code> is 0, <code class=\"nobreak\">d2</code> is 1, <code class=\"nobreak\">d1</code> is 1 and <code class=\"nobreak\">d0</code> is 0. <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> picks which of them reaches <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code>. Steps 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p><code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> copies the input that <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> names. <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> 2 gives <code class=\"nobreak\">d2</code>, which is 1 (steps 2 and 4); <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> 3 gives <code class=\"nobreak\">d3</code>, which is 0 (steps 3 and 6); <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> 0 gives <code class=\"nobreak\">d0</code>, 0 (step 5); <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> 1 gives <code class=\"nobreak\">d1</code>, 1 (step 7). Nothing waits: <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> changes in the same step as <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code>.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"mux4-steps","source":"hdl/level-01/mux4/mux4_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"step","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"sel[1:0]","path":"mux4_tb.sel","width":2,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"00"],[1,"01"],[2,"10"],[3,"11"],[4,"10"],[5,"00"],[6,"11"],[7,"01"]]},{"label":"d[3:0]","path":"mux4_tb.d","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0110"]]},{"label":"y","path":"mux4_tb.y","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[3,"0"],[4,"1"],[5,"0"],[7,"1"]],"samples":["0","1","1","0","1","0","0","1"]}]},"answer":"y","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"mux-fill-cond","itemId":"multiplexer","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> must be <code class=\"nobreak\">b</code> when <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> is 1 and <code class=\"nobreak\">a</code> when <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> is 0. Type what goes after the question mark.","explanationHtml":"<p>The conditional operator gives the value before <code class=\"nobreak\">:</code> when the condition is 1, and the value after it when the condition is 0. So <code class=\"nobreak\">b</code> comes first. Written the other way round, the multiplexer would pass the wrong input for both values of <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code>.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-01/mux2/mux2.sv","firstLine":1,"totalLines":9,"before":["// A 2-to-1 multiplexer: y is b when sel is 1, and a when sel is 0.","module mux2 (","  input  logic sel,","  input  logic a,","  input  logic b,","  output logic y",");"],"blankLine":{"left":"  assign y = sel ? ","right":";"},"after":["endmodule"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"// A 2-to-1 multiplexer: y is b when sel is 1, and a when sel is 0.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"mux2","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" sel,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" a,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" b,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" y","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" y ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" sel ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"?","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]},"after":[[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]]},"accept":["b : a","b: a","b :a","b:a"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The two choices"},{"id":"mux-find-bug","itemId":"multiplexer","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"In mode 1, these LEDs should show the opposite of the switches, but the testbench fails. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p><code>case (mode)</code> runs the line whose label matches, and <code class=\"nobreak\">2'd1</code> is mode 1. That line copies <code class=\"nobreak\">sw</code>, exactly like mode 0. The opposite of the switches is <code class=\"nobreak\">~sw</code>: <code class=\"nobreak\">~</code> turns over each of the four bits (lesson 1.2). The testbench's first failure is mode 1 with every switch at 0, where all four LEDs should be on.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-01/led_mode_bug/led_mode_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// Four pictures on four LEDs, chosen by mode: mode 0 shows the switches,","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// mode 1 the opposite of the switches, mode 2 all LEDs on, mode 3 all off.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"led_mode_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"1","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] mode,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"3","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] sw,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"3","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] led","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"always_comb","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"begin","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"case","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" (mode)","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"      ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"2'd0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"    led ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" sw;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"      ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"2'd1","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"    led ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" sw;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"      ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"2'd2","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"    led ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"4'b1111","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"      ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"default","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" led ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"4'b0000","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"    ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"endcase","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"end","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}],[{"text":"endmodule","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true}]],"bugLine":11,"fixLine":"2'd1:    led = ~sw;"},{"id":"mux-report-lut6","itemId":"multiplexer","role":"core","promptHtml":"Vivado built <code class=\"nobreak\">mux4.sv</code>, which has two select bits and four data bits, for the Arty A7-100T. Below is the Primitives table of its Utilization report: one row for each kind of cell, with how many the design uses. A LUT6 is a LUT that uses all six of its inputs.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the LUT6 row. <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> depends on six inputs, <code class=\"nobreak\">d0</code> to <code class=\"nobreak\">d3</code> and the two bits of <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code>, and a LUT has six, so the whole multiplexer is one LUT6 holding a 64-row truth table. The other rows are the pin buffers: six inputs and one output.</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/mux4/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":180,"excerpt":["+----------+------+---------------------+","| Ref Name | Used | Functional Category |","+----------+------+---------------------+","| IBUF     |    6 |                  IO |","| OBUF     |    1 |                  IO |","| LUT6     |    1 |                 LUT |","+----------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"How many LUT6 cells did Vivado use for mux4?","answer":"1","numeric":true},{"id":"mux-report-lut3","itemId":"multiplexer","role":"core","promptHtml":"Vivado built <code class=\"nobreak\">mux2.sv</code>, the 2-to-1 multiplexer written with the conditional operator, for the Arty A7-100T. Below is the Primitives table of its Utilization report: one row for each kind of cell, with how many the design uses.","explanationHtml":"<p>Read the LUT3 row. <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> depends on three inputs, <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">a</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">b</code>, so one LUT3 holds its eight-row truth table. Synthesis builds the same one LUT3 when the choice is written with <code class=\"nobreak\">if</code> or with <code class=\"nobreak\">case</code> (lesson 1.3).</p>","type":"report","source":"vivado/reports/mux2/arty-a7-100t/utilization.rpt","firstLine":180,"excerpt":["+----------+------+---------------------+","| Ref Name | Used | Functional Category |","+----------+------+---------------------+","| IBUF     |    3 |                  IO |","| OBUF     |    1 |                  IO |","| LUT3     |    1 |                 LUT |","+----------+------+---------------------+"],"ask":"How many LUT3 cells did Vivado use for mux2?","answer":"1","numeric":true},{"id":"mux-predict-mixed","itemId":"multiplexer","role":"core","promptHtml":"The testbench joins bit 0 of its vector <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> to <code class=\"nobreak\">mux4</code>'s <code class=\"nobreak\">d0</code>, bit 1 to <code class=\"nobreak\">d1</code>, and so on up to <code class=\"nobreak\">d3</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> is drawn in hexadecimal. <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> picks which of <code class=\"nobreak\">d0</code> to <code class=\"nobreak\">d3</code> reaches <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code>. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> for every step.","explanationHtml":"<p>Turn each hex digit into its four bits, bit 3 first (lesson 1.1): 9 is 1001, C is 1100, 5 is 0101 and A is 1010. Then <code class=\"nobreak\">y</code> is the bit that <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> names (lesson 1.3). With <code class=\"nobreak\">d</code> at 9, <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> 0 and 3 give 1 and <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> 1 gives 0. With C, <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> 2 gives 1 and <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> 0 gives 0. With 5, <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> 1 gives 0 and <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> 2 gives 1. With A, <code class=\"nobreak\">sel</code> 3 gives 1.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"mux4-mixed","source":"hdl/level-01/mux4/mux4_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"step","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"sel[1:0]","path":"mux4_tb.sel","width":2,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"00"],[1,"11"],[2,"01"],[3,"10"],[4,"00"],[5,"01"],[6,"10"],[7,"11"]]},{"label":"d[3:0]","path":"mux4_tb.d","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1001"],[3,"1100"],[5,"0101"],[7,"1010"]]},{"label":"y","path":"mux4_tb.y","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[2,"0"],[3,"1"],[4,"0"],[6,"1"]],"samples":["1","1","0","1","0","0","1","1"]}]},"answer":"y"}]